Keeps this directory in git, and it has to stay.

The updater's output directory is bind-mounted over this path at runtime, and the
site root above it is mounted read-only. Docker cannot create a mountpoint inside
a read-only mount, so if this directory is missing the uitjes container fails to
start outright:

  error mounting ... to rootfs at "/usr/share/nginx/html/data":
  create mountpoint ...: read-only file system

Nothing here is ever served -- the data mount shadows the whole directory.
